<img src="./_fixtures/sample.png" alt="A sample image" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">

<p>downloads: {{ npmDownloads.downloads }}</p>

{%- comment -%}
Task 12a: an h-feed listing every post, newest first. Deliberately NOT
layouts/page.liquid (the placeholder homepage this replaces used it) — that
layout wraps its whole `{{ content }}` in a single `<article class="h-entry">`,
which would mark the entire homepage as one h-entry containing this h-feed's
own h-entry children: a nested-entry relationship that means something
specific in microformats2 (a post's children, e.g. comments) and is wrong for
a top-level listing. layouts/default.liquid carries no such wrapper.

collections.post is already sorted oldest-first (Eleventy's own default sort,
ascending by date) — `reverse` here, not a second sort, is what gives
newest-first.

Task S4 (audit §2.2): `.posts` is the source's own class carrying the whole
listing's flex-column layout and the two-col-viewport dotted-leader row
(sass/theme-posts.scss) — `h-feed` sits alongside it, not instead of it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<ol class="posts h-feed">
	{%- assign posts = collections.post | reverse -%}
	{%- for post in posts -%}
		{%- include "partials/post-list-entry.liquid", post: post, page: post -%}
	{%- endfor -%}
</ol>
